In `faker/providers/emoji/__init__.py`, `Provider.emoji()` ends with `return self.random_element(self.emojis)`. The test mutates `emojis` to `()`, so `random_element` receives an empty tuple. In `faker/providers/__init__.py`, `random_element` returns `self.random_elements(elements, length=1)[0]`; with no available elements, that result is empty, and indexing `[0]` raises `IndexError` with message `tuple index out of range`.

## Answer
{"exception_message":"tuple index out of range","exception_type":"IndexError"}
